---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data.mjs';
import { orderTerms } from '../../ordering.mjs';
const path = '/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/';
const title = 'Poly Mailer Cost & MOQ: What to Include in a Quote';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title,
  author: { '@id': `${site.origin}/#organization` },
  publisher: { '@id': `${site.origin}/#organization` },
  mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`,
  datePublished: '2026-10-18', dateModified: '2026-11-05', inLanguage: 'en'
};
const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: site.origin },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Buying Guides', item: `${site.origin}/guides/` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Poly mailer cost and MOQ', item: `${site.origin}${path}` }
  ]
};
const brief = `Product / catalogue model:
What will go inside (packed dimensions if known):
Bag dimensions and units (or help needed with sizing):
Quantity for each size and design:
Alternative quantities to compare using the same specification:
Material, closure and protection requirements:
Film thickness and whether this is a single-wall measurement:
Logo / artwork available and print sides:
Sample required:
Please separate product, setup, sample-related and delivery charges:
Destination country, postcode or port:
Required arrival date:
Please confirm the minimum for each version and any pending charges:`;
const costFactors = [
  ['Size and usable fit', 'Catalogue model or proposed outer and usable dimensions, flap allowance and packed item measurements.', 'Use the same dimensions in each quantity option; confirm any proposed size change.'],
  ['Material and film thickness', 'Material description, thickness value, units and whether it measures one wall or another construction.', 'Identify the offered material and measurement convention before comparing prices.'],
  ['Printing and artwork', 'Print sides, artwork version, colors, coverage and placement; ask which print method is offered.', 'Ask which artwork, plate or setup items are included or separately quoted.'],
  ['Quantity and versions', 'Pieces per size, color and artwork, plus any alternative quantities for the same specification.', 'Confirm the minimum and price for each version; a combined total does not establish eligibility.'],
  ['Closure and packing', 'Flap, adhesive or other closure requirements, labels, assortment and carton packing.', 'Identify included packing and any separately quoted requirements.'],
  ['Samples and delivery', 'Sample route, destination, arrival requirement and requested delivery scope.', 'Separate the product price, applicable sample-related items, courier and bulk delivery charges.']
];
---
<Layout title="Poly Mailer Cost & MOQ | Custom Quote Guide | Welltroy" description="Understand the details behind a poly mailer quote: size, film thickness, printing, quantity per design, setup and delivery. Confirm eligible 500-piece minimums." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]} quoteProduct="poly-mailers" contactContext="Poly mailer cost, minimum quantity and itemized quotation">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Cost &amp; MOQ</div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Plan a comparison-ready custom order</p><h1>{title}</h1>
    <p class="lead">Request a poly mailer price against a clear size, material, print design and quantity. Eligible Welltroy bag specifications start from 500 pieces; confirm the minimum for each version and separate the product price from setup, sample-related and delivery charges.</p>
    <p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-05">5 November 2026</time></p>
    <nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#poly-cost">Cost details</a><a href="#minimum">Minimum by version</a><a href="#total-cost">Itemized quote</a><a href="#details">Prepare the details</a><a href="#example">Enquiry example</a><a href="#brief">Use the brief</a></nav>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout">
    <article class="article-main">
      <h2 id="poly-cost">What Determines a Custom Poly Mailer Quote?</h2>
      <p>Ask for a price for your selected <a href="/products/poly-mailers/">poly mailer</a> construction and destination. A unit price is useful when you also know the specification, quantity, currency and included charges. If a requirement is open, ask for it to be identified in the quotation.</p>
      <p class="table-scroll-hint">Swipe or scroll the table to see the quotation details and questions.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Poly mailer cost inputs"><table class="cost-inputs"><caption>Six inputs to confirm before comparing poly mailer prices</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Quote input</th><th scope="col">What to specify</th><th scope="col">What to clarify</th></tr></thead><tbody>{costFactors.map(([factor, specify, clarify]) => <tr><th scope="row">{factor}</th><td>{specify}</td><td>{clarify}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p>Use your <a href="/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/#measurement-record">packed-item measurements</a> to discuss fit, and confirm the <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#poly-mailer-printing">film and printing specification</a> before comparing quantity options. Include any <a href="/materials-and-documents/#document-request">material document requirements</a> in the initial brief so availability can be checked.</p>
      <h2 id="minimum">What Does “From 500 Pieces” Mean?</h2>
      <p>The available size, material, printing and construction need to be confirmed for your order. Do not assume that 500 pieces can be divided across several sizes, colors or artworks and still qualify for the same minimum. List the split and ask us to confirm the minimum for each specification.</p>
      <h3>Confirm the Minimum for Each Size, Color and Artwork</h3><p>List each version on a separate line. The following quantities illustrate how to describe a request; they are not confirmed offers or guaranteed minimums.</p><ul><li><strong>One version:</strong> 500 pieces in one size and one artwork. Ask whether that construction is eligible and what the quoted minimum includes.</li><li><strong>Two artworks:</strong> 250 pieces of artwork A and 250 of artwork B. Ask for the minimum and setup scope for each artwork; the total of 500 alone does not confirm eligibility.</li><li><strong>Two sizes:</strong> 500 pieces in each size. Request a separate quantity, specification and price for each line.</li></ul>
      <p>If you want quantity alternatives, ask for the same specification at your proposed starting quantity and a second quantity, such as 500 and 1,000 pieces where eligible. Compare the confirmed unit prices, product totals and additional charges. Ask for the minimum for a repeat order separately rather than assuming the initial terms remain available.</p>
      <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Check the sales unit.</strong> Bags and mailers start from 500 pieces for eligible specifications. Honeycomb paper starts from 1 roll (1 pc). Thermal labels need the roll or fanfold configuration and sales unit confirmed separately. This guide does not promise every packaging format at a 500-piece minimum.</div>
      <h2 id="details">Six Details That Make a Quote Useful</h2>
      <h3>1. Product and intended use</h3><p>Name the catalogue model or link to the product page. Explain what goes inside and how you pack it. If you are deciding between a plain mailer and a cushioned format, describe the contents and protection needs. Our <a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">mailer selection guide</a> can help you frame that question.</p>
      <h3>2. Dimensions, with units and measurement notes</h3><p>Write dimensions in mm or cm and identify width, height, gusset and flap where relevant. Say whether the figures describe the outside of the bag, the usable space or the packed contents. If you only know the packed item size, send that rather than guessing a bag size. A catalogue dimension is a reference to confirm, not a fit guarantee.</p>
      <h3>3. Quantity for each size and design</h3><p>Separate the quantity for each version. “500 pieces, one size, one design” is different from “250 pieces of each of two designs.” If you want price comparisons, request alternative quantities using the same specification so the quotations can be compared.</p>
      <h3>4. Material, closure and printing requirements</h3><p>Describe any required thickness, paper weight, closure, finish or print sides. If these are not decided, explain the job the packaging must do. Send the logo or an artwork preview and tell us whether an editable file is available. Ask for the applicable print template, safe area, bleed and color requirements before preparing final production artwork.</p>
      <p>For food contact or environmental requirements, identify the exact intended use and destination market. Ask for documents for the proposed material and construction; a product name, image or generic claim is not enough to confirm suitability.</p>
      <h3>5. Sample route</h3><p>Tell us whether you want an existing product sample to review construction, or a custom printed sample to assess your artwork and specification. Samples are free; confirm availability, preparation, artwork or setup arrangements and courier charges. Free samples do not automatically include free delivery.</p>
      <h3>6. Destination and arrival deadline</h3><p>Include the country and postcode or port, plus any required arrival date. Ask for production and transport estimates separately. {orderTerms.production} Freight, duties and taxes should be identified in the quotation rather than assumed to be included.</p>
      <h2 id="example">Example: A Clear 500-piece Mailer Enquiry</h2>
      <p>This is an illustrative brief, not a completed customer project or a confirmed specification:</p>
      <blockquote>We are comparing 500 poly mailers in one size and one artwork for folded clothing. The packed item measures 24 × 30 × 4 cm. Please recommend a suitable bag size and confirm usable space, material, closure and logo printing options. We have an editable AI logo and need a sample before confirming the bulk order. Delivery is to our stated country and postcode; please quote production and transport separately.</blockquote>
      <p>The packed measurements in this example are not a recommended bag size. In your own enquiry, replace them with your measurements and include your actual destination and timing.</p>
      <h2 id="total-cost">Request an Itemized Quotation</h2>
      <p>Ask the quotation to identify the product unit price and quantity for each version, currency, applicable setup, sample-related items, packing and delivery. Confirm whether each additional item is included, charged separately, estimated, excluded or still pending.</p>
      <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Use confirmed amounts for the same scope.</strong><p>Product amount = quoted unit price × quoted quantity for each version. Add the applicable, confirmed setup, sample-related, packing and delivery items once. Keep currencies separate and ask which destination charges, duties or taxes are included. An unknown charge remains pending; treating it as zero makes the comparison incomplete.</p></div>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Packaging quotation comparison checklist"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Confirm in writing</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Specification</td><td>Size, usable dimensions, material, closure, print and artwork reference</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Quantity</td><td>Pieces per size and design, packing and the agreed minimum</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Costs</td><td>Packaging, any setup or sample charges, freight, duties and taxes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Timing</td><td>Approval steps, production start milestone, dispatch and transit estimates</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Payment</td><td>T/T: 30% deposit and 70% balance; confirm the balance milestone in the written quotation</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <p>Ask whether any setup item applies again to a repeat order, and whether a quantity or artwork change requires a revised quote. Once you receive proposals, use the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/#worksheet">quotation comparison worksheet</a> to check that specification and delivery scope match before comparing totals.</p>
      <p>See <a href="/ordering/">samples, payment and delivery</a> for the current ordering process. Submitting an enquiry requests a quotation; it does not place an order or take payment.</p>
      <h2 id="brief">Your Ready-to-use Quote Brief</h2><p>Prefer to prepare the request on the product page? <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">Add alternative quantities, destination postal code and an itemized delivery quote request</a>. Your selected size, artwork and existing notes stay in the same editable brief.</p><p>Copy the prompts below into your enquiry. Mark unknown details as “please advise” and include a reply email.</p>
      <pre class="quote-brief">{brief}</pre>
      <p>The website accepts AI, PSD, PDF, PNG, JPG, WEBP, DOCX, XLSX, TXT and CSV files: up to three files, with a combined limit of 10 MB. File acceptance does not confirm that artwork is ready to print. Keep the original editable file and ask us to review it.</p>
      <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=poly-mailers#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request an Itemized Poly Mailer Quote</a><a class="text-link" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Discuss other packaging formats →</a></div>
      <h2>Questions About Poly Mailer Cost and Minimums</h2><h3>Does a 500-piece total cover several artworks?</h3><p>List the pieces for each artwork and size, then confirm the minimum for each version. A combined quantity is not confirmation of eligibility.</p><h3>Does a larger quantity always give a lower delivered cost?</h3><p>Request written quantity options using the same specification and destination. Compare the confirmed product amount and additional charges, as well as the quantity you actually need.</p><h3>Is a sample courier charge included in the unit price?</h3><p>Ask the quotation to identify the sample type, what is free and any applicable preparation, setup or courier arrangements. Confirm these before dispatch rather than assuming they are part of the bulk unit price.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Start with a product</p><h2>Related Packaging</h2><div class="guide-options">
      <a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Clothing and other lightweight, non-fragile goods</span></a>
      <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Compare cushioning, closure and usable inner space</span></a>
      <a href="/products/kraft-paper-bags/"><strong>Kraft Paper Bags</strong><span>Retail presentation, bag dimensions and handle requirements</span></a>
    </div><p>Confirm the eligible specification and minimum for your project.</p><a class="text-link" href="/ordering/">Review the order steps →</a></aside>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .article-main {min-width:0;}
  .article-main h3 {margin:28px 0 12px;}
  .article-main blockquote {margin:24px 0;padding:20px 24px;border-left:4px solid var(--orange);background:var(--cream);line-height:1.8;}
  .quote-brief {white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--cream);font:inherit;line-height:1.8;}
  .article-main td {min-width:140px;vertical-align:top;}
  .cost-inputs{min-width:760px;}.cost-inputs th,.cost-inputs td{vertical-align:top;min-width:180px;}.cost-inputs th[scope="row"]{min-width:140px;}.article-main .button{white-space:normal;text-align:center;}
  h2[id] {scroll-margin-top:120px;}
</style>
